hadiths[94]{hadithnumber,text}:
"7423","Abu Bakr Ahmad bin Salman al-Faqih told us in Baghdad, and Abu Ahmad Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us in Marw, they said: Abu Qalabah told us Abdul Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqashi, Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Al-Rukain bin Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Qais bin Muslim, on the authority of Tariq Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: “God has not sent down a disease except that He has sent down a cure for it, and in the milk of cows.” A cure for every disease.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Abu Abd al-Rahman al-Sulami and Tariq ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah bin Masoud
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7423 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7424","So Abu Ahmad Al-Hussein bin Ali Al-Tamimi told us, Abdullah bin Muhammad Al-Baghawi told me, my grandfather Ahmed bin Mani’ told me, narrated to me. Ubaidah bin Humaid, Ata bin Al-Sa’ib told us, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “Allah has not sent down a disease but He has also sent down with it a cure, which those who knew it knew about it and those who were ignorant of it knew about it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7424 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7425","So Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub, Al-Adl told us, Muhammad bin Abdul-Wahhab Al-Farra informed us, Ja’far bin Aoun informed us, Al-Masoudi informed us, about Qais bin Muslim Al-Jadli, on the authority of Tariq bin Shihab, on the authority of Abdullah, referring it to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: “Indeed, God Almighty did not send down disease, unless He sends down a cure for it, except old age. So you should drink cow’s milk, for it comes from every tree.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7425 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7426","Ishaq bin Muhammad bin Khalid Al-Hashimi told us, in Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, he informed us Israel, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father, he said: I said to Aisha, may God be pleased with her: I took the Sunnahs from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. And poetry and Arabic are from the Arabs. Who did you take medicine from? She said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was a sick man, and Arab doctors used to come to him, so I could learn from them.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7426 - Sahih according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7427","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hasan bin Qutaybah told us, Muhammad bin Hashim told us, Suwayd bin Abdul Aziz told us, Issa told me Ibn Abd al-Rahman, he said: I heard Zurr ibn Hubaysh, speaking on the authority of Safwan ibn Assal al-Muradi, he said: They said: O Messenger of God, have you sought medical treatment? He said: “Do you know that God Almighty has not sent down a disease without sending down a cure for it, other than one disease?” They said: What is it? He said: “Al-Haram” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7427 - True"
"7428","Ismail ibn Muhammad ibn al-Fadl ibn Muhammad al-Sha’arani told me, my grandfather told me, Yahya ibn Sulayman al-Ja’fi told me, Ibn Wahb told me, Ibrahim bin Tahman told me, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “When Suleiman bin Dawood, peace and blessings be upon him, rose during Ramadan, he saw a tree growing in front of him and said: What is your name? So you say: Such and such, and he says: What are you for? So you say: For such and such. If it was for a cure, it would be written down, and if it was for a planting, it would be planted. While he was praying one day, behold, a tree A plant grew in his hands, and he said to her: What is your name? She said: The carob. He said: What are you for? She said: Because of the ruin of the people of this house. So Solomon, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Oh God, make my death cause grief to the jinn so that mankind may know that the jinn do not know the unseen. He said: So he carved it out as a stick and it leaned on it for a dead year while the jinn were working and the earth devoured it and it fell. When it fell down, mankind realized that the jinn were They do not know the unseen.” He said: “Then the jinn thanked the earth and used to bring it water.” And Ibn Abbas used to read it like this. “This is a hadith. The chain of narration is authentic, but they did not narrate it. It is somewhat strange than the narration of Ubayd Allah ibn Wahb on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Tahman, for I do not find anything from him other than the narration of this hadith. “The One.” It was narrated by Salamah bin Kuhail, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, so he attributed it to Ibn Abbas.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7428 - Sahih Gharib Bumrah"
"7429","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Abdul-Jabbar bin Al-Abbas told us Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Salamah ibn Kuhail, on the authority of Saeed ibn Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: “Sulaiman ibn Dawud was in charge of them.” Prayer and peace: When he prays the prayer, a tree appears before his eyes, and he says to it: What are you, and for what purpose does it appear, and it says: I am the tree of such-and-such? I appeared for such-and-such illness. One morning, when he prayed, a tree appeared before his eyes. He said to it: What are you and for what purpose did you appear? I, the shepherd, rose to destroy this mosque, so Solomon, peace and blessings be upon him, knew that his time had approached and that the Holy House would not be destroyed. While he was alive, he prayed to God Almighty to cause Satan to pass out due to his death. The jinn were claiming that the devils know the unseen, so he died on his staff. Then the earth devoured it, and it fell, so it was the duty of the devils to bring water to the earth, as they had praised it in thanks for what they had done with the rod of Solomon. """
"7430","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Ali bin Muhammad Al-Tanafisi told us, Mas’ar told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin relationship, and Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Shafi’i told me, Ibrahim bin Ishaq told us, Ishaq told us, and Othman bin Abi Shaybah told us, They said: Jarir told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, Abdullah bin Omar Al-Jawhari told us, with Marwa, Abdullah bin Ahmad told us Ibn Hanbal, Ibrahim bin Al-Hajjaj told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and Abu Bakr told us Bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Khaythamah told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah Al-Ja’fi told us, On the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and Abu Al-Hasan Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Sunni informed us, about Marwa, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdan informed us, Abu Hamza told me, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, and Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told me, Ishaq bin Al-Hassan told me, Abdullah bin Please, Israel told us, Ziyad bin Ulaqah told us, and Abu Bakr al-Shafi’i told us, Muhammad bin Bishr, brother of Khattab told us, Muhammad told us. Ibn Al-Sabbah, Asbat Ibn Nasr told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Ziyad Ibn Ulaqah, and Ahmad Ibn Ja’far Al-Quta’i informed us,Abdullah bin Ahmad bin Hanbal told us, my father told us, Al-Muttalib bin Ziyad told us, Ziyad bin Ulaqah told us, and Ahmad bin Othman Al-Adami, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Maslamah Al-Wasiti told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Masoudi reported, on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah, Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih, Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl, and Abu Bakr Al-Shafi’i told us, they said: The wording for them is: Bishr bin Musa, Al-Humaidi told us, Sufyan told us, Ziyad bin Ulaqah told me, he said: I heard Usama bin Sharik Al-Amiri saying: I witnessed the Bedouins asking The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, is there a burden on us in such-and-such? He said: “Servants of God, God has placed the burden on us, except for the one who borrowed from his brother’s honor.” “Something, that is what caused hardship and destruction.” They said: O Messenger of God, shall we seek medical treatment? He said: “Take care, servants of God, for God Almighty has not sent down a disease without having sent down a cure for it, except this old man.” They said: O Messenger of God, how good What was given to the Muslim servant? He said: “Good character.” This is a hadith whose chains of transmission are all authentic, according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. They did not narrate it, and the reason they have for it is that Usama bin Sharik It has no narrator other than Ziyad bin Ulaqah.It was proven at the beginning of this book with arguments, proofs and evidence from them that this is not a cause, and there are remaining ways of this “The hadith on the authority of Ziyad bin Ulaqah is more than what I mentioned, since the narration was not according to their conditions.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7430 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7431","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us, in Hamdan, Ishaq bin Ibrahim al-Kharraz told us, Ishaq bin Sulayman told us, Salih bin Al-Akhdar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Hakim ibn Hazzam, said: I said: O Messenger of God, have you seen medicines that we use to treat themselves with ruqyah? We seek refuge through it. Are you rejecting God’s decree? He said: “It is from God’s decree.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Yunus bin Yazid and Omar bin Al-Harith,” with a chain of transmission. Another, and it is the preserved one.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7431 - True"
"7432","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, and Yunus bin Yazid, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, that Abu Khuzama bin Yamar, one of the Banu Al-Harith bin Saad, narrated to him, that his father narrated to him that he said to the Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: O Messenger of God, have you seen a medicine with which we can be treated and a ruqyah with which we can pray for guidance? Does this reject anything from God’s decree? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “It is God’s decree.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7432 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7433","Abu Abdul Rahman Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Tajer told me, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Ansari told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Amr, on the authority of Abu Salamah, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Indeed, He who sent down the disease sent down Al-Shifa’ This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7433 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7434","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abdul Rabbuh bin Saeed, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir bin Abdullah, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, that he said: “For every disease there is a cure, so if the cure strikes the disease, it will be cured, God Almighty willing.” This is an authentic hadith according to the condition of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7434 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7435","Abu Ali Al-Hussein told us, and Abu Muhammad Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz narrated to us, saying: Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah narrated to us, narrated to us Ali bin Salamah, by memorization, Zayd bin Al-Hubab told us, Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, may God be pleased with him. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “You must use the two cures: honey and the Qur’an.” This is an authentic chain of transmission according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it. It was narrated by Waki` ibn al-Jarrah, on the authority of Sufyan
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7435 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7436","Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Qutaybah told us, Abu Bakr bin Abi Shaybah told us, Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, said: Abdullah said: “There are two cures: reading the Qur’an and drinking honey.”"
"7437","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Affan told us, Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Khaythamah, And Al-Aswad, they said: Abdullah said: “You should use the two cures: the Qur’an and honey.”"
"7438","Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told me, Al-Fadl bin Muhammad Al-Shaarani told us, Ubayd Allah bin Muhammad bin Aisha told us, Hammad bin Salamah told us, On the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas ibn Malik, may God be pleased with him, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “If one of you has a fever, let him pour cold water over him.” “Three nights of dawn.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim. They did not narrate it, but rather they agreed on the chain of narrations that the fever is from the stench of Hell. So extinguish it with water.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7438 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7439","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hasan Al-Hamdani, and Hisham bin Ali Al-Sirafi told us, they said: Abdullah bin Raja told us, Hammam bin Yahya narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Jamra al-Dhab’i, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Abbas in Mecca, and he missed me for days, and when I came he said: What He imprisoned you? He said: I said: I took a bath, and he said: Cool it off from you with Zamzam water, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Fever is from the stench of Hell.” “So cool it with Zamzam water.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this context.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7439 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7440","Abu Ja`far Muhammad bin Muhammad al-Baghdadi told us, Yahya bin Uthman bin Saleh told us, in Egypt, Sa`id bin Abi Maryam told us, he informed us Abdullah bin Farukh, Ibn Jurayj told me, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of Uqba Al-Zarqi, on the authority of Zur’ah bin Abdullah bin Ziyad, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, May God be pleased with him. He told him about Asma bint Umays, may God be pleased with her, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon her one day. Then she knocked on a shambar and said, “What are you doing with this?” She said: So-and-so drinks it, and he said: “If anything wards off death or benefits from death, it would benefit from the Sunnah.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but it is not “He narrates it” and there is evidence for it from the hadith of the Basraites on the authority of Asma’ bint Umays, may God be pleased with her.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7440 - True"
"7441","Abu Muhammad al-Hasan bin Muhammad al-Isfaraini told us, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Raja al-Sindi told us, al-Abbas bin Abdul-Azeem told us. Al-Anbari, Abu Bakr Al-Hanafi told us, Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar told us, Utbah bin Abdullah al-Taymi told me, on the authority of Asma bint Umays, May God be pleased with her. The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, asked her: “What are you showering with?” She said: I was brushing with shamrock. He said: “Hot, hot.” She said: Then I was brushing with senna, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If only “Something in which there was recovery from death would have been the Sunnah.”"
"7442","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bakr bin Sahl Al-Damiati told us, Omar bin Bakr Al-Saskiki told us, Ibrahim bin Abi told us Abla, he said: I heard Abu Ubayy ibn Umm Hazzam, who had prayed the two prayers with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace God, peace and blessings be upon him, says: “Adhere to the Sunnah and the Sunnah, for in them is a cure for every disease except the poison.” It was said: O Messenger of God, and what is the poison? He said: “Death.” Ibrahim bin Abi Abla said: “And the sunnoot: dill.” Amr bin Bakr said, and others say: “The sunnoon is the honey that is In Al-Ziq, which is what the poet said:
[Long Sea]

They are fat with tongues, there is no good in them... and they prevent the neighbor from being naked.”
This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7442 - Amr bin Bakr was accused by Ibn Hibban"
"7443","Ahmad bin Kamil Al-Qadi told us, Muhammad bin Saad Al-Awfi told us, Amr bin Muhammad bin Abi Razin told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hudha’, on the authority of Maimun Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded us to seek treatment from... Pleurisy with sea costus and oil” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Qatada, on the authority of Maymun Abi Abd God
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7443 - True"
"7444","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Muadh bin Hisham told us, my father told me, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Abu Abdullah, on the authority of Zaid bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, calling: “Oil And the lump is from pleurisy.” Qatada said: “He gives birth with it from the side that complains.” It was narrated by Abd al-Rahman ibn Maymun, on the authority of his father.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7444 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7445","Abdullah bin Ishaq Al-Khurasani told us, Abdul-Malik bin Muhammad Al-Raqqashi told us, Yaqoub bin Ishaq Al-Hadrami told us, Abdul told me Al-Rahman bin Maimun, my father told me, on the authority of Zayd bin Arqam, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, described to us a pleurisy. “rice, oil, and wheat.”"
"7446","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani informed us, in Mecca, Ishaq bin Ibrahim informed us, Abdul Razzaq informed us, Muammar informed us, On the authority of Al-Zuhri, Abu Bakr bin Abdul Rahman bin Al-Harith bin Hisham told me, on the authority of Asma bint Umays, may God be pleased with her, who said: The first time the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, complained was in Bayt Maimuna, and his pain became severe until he fainted. He said: So the women of his town took advice and gave him pain. He woke up and said: “This is not the action of the women who came from here.” He pointed to the land of Abyssinia, where there was Asma bint Umays, and they said: Their kinana. You are suffering from a state of sexual impurity, O Messenger of God. He said: “This is an illness that God would not have slandered me with. No one will remain in the house except a child except the uncle of the Messenger of God,” meaning Abbas. He said: “On that day, Maimunah went to marriage, and she was fasting according to the determination of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the condition. The two sheikhs did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7446 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7447","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Ismail bin Ishaq Al-Qadi told us, and Ali bin Abdul Aziz Al-Baghawi told us, he said: Suleiman bin Daoud told us. Al-Hashimi, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Zinad told me, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, my father told me that Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: Oh My nephew, I saw that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, venerating his uncle was a strange thing. This is because the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, The middle part takes it and becomes strong with it. We used to say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took the vein of the kidney, but we are not guided by saying: The middle part. She took the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, one day and made him feel anxious until he fainted. We became afraid for him, and the people became frightened towards him, so we thought that something was wrong with him. He was in a state of impurity, so We gave him birth. Then he walked away from the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he recovered and realized that he had given birth, and he found traces of that childbirth and said: “Did you think that God had given it authority over me? God would not have given it authority over me, by the One in Whose Hand is my soul. No one shall remain in the house except a child, except my uncle.” He said: I saw them giving birth to them, man by man. Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “And whoever is in the House that Day, We will remember their virtue, will give birth.” All the men, and Al-Laddud reached the wives of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and they gave birth to woman after woman, until Al-Laddud reached a woman among us.” Abu Al-Zinad said: “And I do not know of her as anything other than Maimunah.” He said: “And the people said: Umm Salamah said: By God, I am fasting. So we said: It is miserable, by God. I did not think that We leave you, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, swore, so we told her, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7447 - True"
"7448","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Yahya bin Hassan told us, Wahib bin Khalid told us, Abdullah bin Tawus, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, begged.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs. And they did not bring it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7448 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7449","Muhammad ibn Ibrahim ibn al-Fadl al-Muzaki narrated to us, Ibrahim ibn Abi Talib narrated to us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad narrated to us, my father narrated to me, Al-Mish’al bin Amr told us, on the authority of Amr bin Sulaym, on the authority of Rafi’ bin Amr, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The stick, the rock, and the tree are from Paradise.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7449 - True"
"7450","Abu Sahl Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Ziyad Al-Qattan told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Ubaid bin Waqid bin Al-Qasim Al-Qaisi, Othman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Abdi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, that a delegation Abd al-Qais, one of the people of Hijr, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and while they were sitting with him, he approached them and said to them: “A date you call such-and-such and a date you call such-and-such.” Until he counted all the colors of their dates, then a man from among the people said to him: May my mother and father be sacrificed for you. O Messenger of God, if I had been born in the middle of the desert, I would not have learned more than you at this time. I bear witness that you are the Messenger of God. He said: “Indeed, your land has been raised for me.” Since you sat before me and I looked from one end to the other, the best of your dates is the one that removes disease, but there is no disease in it.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration. And they did not bring it out.” And there is evidence for it from the hadith of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7450 - The hadith is objectionable"
"7451","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Zaid bin Al-Hubab told us, Saeed bin Suwayd Al-Samiri told us, Khalid bin Rabah Al-Basri, on the authority of Abu Al-Siddiq Al-Naji, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Good Your dates bring out the disease, but there is no disease in it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7451 - We produced it as a witness"
"7452","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq Al-Faqih and Abu Muhammad bin Musa Al-Adl told us, saying: Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid informed us, Al-Mu’afah told us. Bin Sulaiman, Fulayh bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Ayyub bin Abdul Rahman bin Sa`sa’ah, on the authority of Yaqoub bin Abi Yaqoub, on the authority of Umm al-Mundhir Al-Ansariyya, may God be pleased with her. She was one of the aunts of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. She said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered upon me and was with him. Ali, may God be pleased with him, was convalescing from an illness, and in the house there were stalks hanging, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, got up and ate from it, and Ali came to eat from it. He said: “Leave him, for he will not agree with you, for you are a camel.” So I got up to barley and boiled Swiss chard and brought it to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. Then the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “O Ali, eat of this, and it will be more appropriate for you.” It was narrated by Zayd bin Al-Hubab, on the authority of Fulayh bin Suleiman, and he said: On the authority of Umm Mubashir Al-Ansariyya,"
"7453","Abu Bakr ibn Ishaq informed us, Ahmad ibn Salamah informed me, Ishaq informed me, Zayd ibn al-Hubab informed me, Fulayh ibn Sulaiman told me. Al-Madani, Ayyub ibn Abd al-Rahman al-Ansari informed me, Ya`qub ibn Abi Ya`qub informed me, on the authority of Umm Mubashir al-Ansariyyah, Radi On her authority, some of the aunts of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered upon me, and with him was Ali who was recovering from an illness. So he mentioned the hadith something like, “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7452 - True"
"7454","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, Musaddad told us, Ismail bin Ulayya told us, Muhammad told us Ibn Al-Sa'ib Ibn Baraka Al-Makki, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, took His family was ill. He ordered soup, and it was made. Then he ordered them to taste some of it, and he said: “It is to soothe the heart of the sad and comfort the heart of the sick.” Just as you wiped the dirt from her face with water.”"
"7455","Abu Abdullah told us, Yahya bin Muhammad told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Ayman Al-Makki saying: Fatima bint told me Al-Mundhir, on the authority of Umm Kulthum, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must use the abominable and the beneficial one, the talbinah. By the One in whose hand is the soul of Muhammad, he washes the stomach of one of you just as he washes dirt from his face with water.” He said: And the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was If one of his family complains, the twine will not remain on the fire until one of its two parties is eliminated, either death or life. “This is an authentic hadith on the authority of The condition of the two sheikhs: Muslim cited Muhammad ibn al-Sa’ib as evidence, and Al-Bukhari cited Ayman ibn Nabil al-Makki as evidence, then they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7455 - True"
"7456","Abu Al-Hasan Ali bin Muhammad bin Uqba Al-Shaybani told us about Kufa, Ibrahim bin Ishaq Al-Zuhri told us, Muhammad told us, and Ya’la, Ibn Ubaid said: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, who said: He was with the Mother of the Believers Aisha, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of a boy with blood dripping from his nostrils, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, entered and said: “What is the matter with this boy?” She said: By him is an excuse, so he said: “Woe to you, O women! Do not kill your children, nor any woman who is afflicted by an excuse or a headache. So let her take an Indian portion.” He said: He ordered Aisha, and she did that, and he was healed. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.” Al-Bukhari also narrated the hadith of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubayd Allah bin Abdullah, on the authority of Umm Qais bint Muhsin, with a summary like this.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7456 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7457","Muhammad bin Ali bin Duhaim Al-Shaybani told us, Ahmad bin Hazim bin Abi Gharza told us, Abu Nu’aym told us, Nasr bin Abi told us Al-Ash'ath said: I heard Abu Al-Zubayr mentioning on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him, that a woman brought her son to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So she said: Take away the excuse from him, so he said: “Burn the throats of your children. Take an Indian gorse and a horse and give it to him.” This is an authentic hadith. On the condition of a Muslim, and they did not produce it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7457 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7458","Abu Hafs Omar bin Hatim Al-Faqih told us in Bukhara, Salih bin Muhammad bin Habib Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Aban told us, Abu Amir told us Abd al-Malik bin Amr, Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawwal told us, Ayoub bin al-Hassan bin Ali told me, Ibn Abi Rafi’ told us, on the authority of his grandmother Salma, she said: I never heard anyone complain to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, about pain in his legs except that he said: “Dye them with henna.” This is A hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it. Al-Bukhari, may God have mercy on him, cited Abd al-Rahman bin Abi al-Mawwal as evidence.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7458 - True"
"7459","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Shabib Al-Maamari told us, Ali bin Sahl Al-Ramli told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Hisham bin Hassan told us, Anas bin Sirin told me, Anas bin Malik told me, may God be pleased with him, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cure for sciatica comes from an Arabian sheep that is thawed, then divided into three parts and drunk within three days.” This is an authentic hadith subject to the conditions. The two sheikhs did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman, on the authority of Hisham bin Hassan, with an addition to the text.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7459 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7460","Ali bin Hamshadh Al-Adl told us, Abu Al-Muthanna Al-Anbari told us, Musaddad told us, Al-Mu’tamir told us, he said: I heard Hisham bin Hassan, narrating On the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, he mentioned, “The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, described from the sciatica the buttocks of an Arabian sheep that were not In small or large amounts, it should be melted, then divided into three parts, and drunk one part every day on an empty stomach.” Anas said: “I have described that.” For three hundred, all of them may God Almighty protect him.” It was narrated by Habib bin Al-Shahid, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him."
"7461","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Muhammad bin Al-Hussein bin Makram told us, Al-Abbas bin Yazid Al-Bahrani told us, Abdul Khaleq bin Abi told us Al-Mukhariq Al-Ansari, Habib bin Al-Shahid told us, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God mentioned May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and he said: “The calf of an Arabian ram is taken, neither small nor large, and is thawed and drunk for three days.” Anas bin Malik said: “I described him to more than three hundred, all of whom disavowed him.” These chains of narrations are all authentic on one condition. The Two Sheikhs - “Hammad bin Salamah narrated it, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin, and he said: On the authority of his brother Ma’bad, on the authority of a man, from the Ansar, on the authority of his father, “The opinion we have regarding it is the saying of Al-Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman and Al-Walid bin Muslim.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7461 - True"
"7462","Abu Al-Hussein Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Tamim Al-Handali told us in Baghdad, Abu Qalaba told us, Abu Asim told us, Uthman bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Salem bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “You must be careful, for it makes hair grow and eyesight clear.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7462 - True"
"7463","Abu Bakr Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail Al-Faqih told us about Al-Ray, Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Al-Faraj Al-Azraq told us, in Baghdad, we told us Hajjaj bin Muhammad al-Masisi, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, Amr bin Yahya bin Amara bin Abi Hassan told me, Maryam bint Iyas bin Al-Bukayr, the companion of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on the authority of some of the wives of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and I think it was Zainab, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered On her, he said: “Do you have any offspring?” She said: Yes, so he called for it and put it on a blister between two of his toes and said: “O God, who extinguishes the great and magnifies the small.” Turn it off from me.” It was turned off. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7463 - True"
"7464","Da'laj bin Ahmad al-Sijzi told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muawiyah al-Basri told us, Muhammad bin Jahdham told us, Ismail bin Jafar told us, On the authority of Amara bin Ghaziyah, on the authority of Asim bin Omar bin Qatada, on the authority of Mahmoud bin Labid, on the authority of Qatada bin Al-Numan, may God be pleased with him, that The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If God loves a servant, he protects him in this world just as one of you protects a sick person from water.” This is an authentic hadith. ""
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7464 - True"
"7465","Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Muhammad bin Shazan Al-Jawhari told us, Saeed bin Suleiman Al-Wasiti told us, Muslim bin Khalid told us, Zaid bin Aslam, on the authority of his father, said: “During the time of Omar bin Al-Khattab, I fell seriously ill, so Omar called a doctor for me, and he protected me until I was sucking the seeds from “Severe fever” was explained by Amr bin Abi Amr, the client of al-Muttalib, in his narration, on the authority of Asim bin Amr bin Qatada.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7465 - True"
"7466","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr Al-Khawlani told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, Bukayr bin Abdullah told him that Asim bin Omar bin Qatada told him that Jabir bin Abdullah returned Al-Muqna’ and then said: I will not leave. Until he uses cupping, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, say: “Indeed, there is healing in it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7466 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7467","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Mahmoud Al-Mahboubi told us about Marwa, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Shayban bin Abd told us Al-Rahman, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, on the authority of Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, who said: Bedouins from Bani Fazara entered From the Banu Umm Qarfa, the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and suddenly a cupper was sizing him with cups he had from the horns, marking with a razor, and he said: What This, O Messenger of God, why do you let this break your skin? He said: “This is the size and it is the best of what you have been treated with.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “It was narrated by Shu’bah bin Al-Hajjaj Al-Atki, and Zuhair bin Muawiyah Al-Jafi, on the authority of Abdul-Malik bin Umair
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7467 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7468","So Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji told us, Abd al-Warith bin Abd al-Samad told us, my father told me, Shu’bah told us, On the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Umair, who said: I heard Husayn ibn Abi al-Hurr, speaking on the authority of Samurah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “The best thing is “You treated with it the size.” As for the hadith of Zuhayr"
"7469","So Muhammad bin Saleh bin Hani told us, Ahmad bin Muhammad bin Nasr said: Abu Nu’aym told us, Zuhayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, Husayn ibn al-Hurr narrated to me, on the authority of Samurah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, something similar.
It was narrated by Dawud bin Nusayr Al-Tai, on the authority of Abd Al-Malik bin Umair. Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Akhram told us, Yahya bin Muhammad bin Yahya, Musaddad told us, Ismail Ibn Ulayyah told us, Dawud bin Nusayr told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, on the authority of Husayn bin Abi al-Hurr, on the authority of Samurah, may God be pleased with him, said: A Bedouin from Banu Fazara, from Banu Umm Qarfa, entered the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and behold, Hijam He used cups that he had for centuries, using a razor, and said: What is this, O Messenger of God? Why do you let this cut your skin? He said: “This size.” He said: What is the size? He said: “The best thing that people seek treatment with.”"
"7470","Nusayr bin Muhammad bin Khattab told us, in Baghdad, Muhammad bin Ghalib bin Harb told us, Zakaria bin Adi told us, Ubaid Allah bin Amr told us Al-Ruqi, on the authority of Zayd bin Abi Anisa, on the authority of Muhammad bin Qais, Abu Al-Hakam Al-Bajli, who is Abdul-Rahman bin Abi Na’am, told us: I entered upon Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, was cupping, and he said to me: O Abu Al-Hakam, use cupping. He said: So I said: I have never cupped. “Abu Al-Qasim, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told me that Gabriel, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, told him that size is the best way to heal people.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7470 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7471","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Muhammad bin Ismail told us, Usayd bin Zaid Al-Hammal told us, Zuhayr bin Muawiyah told us, On the authority of Ubayd Allah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If it is in any of what you treat With it there is a cure, such as a cup of cup, or a drink of honey, or a cautery that affects, and I do not like it when it is covered. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not “He brings him out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7471 - Usayd bin Zaid Al-Himmal is abandoned"
"7472","Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Atki told us, Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Anas Al-Qurashi told us, Abu Asim told us, Abbad bin Mansour told us, about Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best thing with which you can cure snuff and evil things is “And cupping and walking.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7472 - Abbad bin Mansur is weak"
"7473","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, May God be pleased with them both. He said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “I did not pass by a group of angels on the night I was taken on the Journey except that they said, ‘You have “By cupping, O Muhammad.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7473 - True"
"7474","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Al-Rabi’ bin Sulayman told us, Shuaib bin Al-Layth told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him. “Aisha, the wife of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, permission to perform cupping, so the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered He asked Abu Taybah to cup her. He said: I thought he said: “And her brother was through breastfeeding or a boy of his who had not had a wet dream.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7474 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7475","Al-Hussein bin Al-Hasan bin Ayyub told us, Abu Hatim Al-Razi told us, Abu Tawbah Al-Rabi’ bin Nafi’ told us, Saeed bin Abdul Rahman told us Al-Jumahi, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who “He used cupping for the seventeenth of the month, and he was cured of every disease.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7475 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7476","Mukarram bin Ahmad Al-Qadi told us, Al-Hasan bin Mukarram told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Abbad bin Mansour told us, on the authority of Ikrimah, On the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The best thing for you to use cupping on is the seventeenth day and the day of “The nineteenth and the twenty-first.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7476 - True"
"7477","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Amr bin Asim Al-Kalabi told us, Hammam bin Yahya told us, And Jarir bin Hazim, they said: Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Anas bin Malik, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to protest against Al-Akha’ain, and he used to perform cupping on the seventeen, nineteen, and twenty-one days. This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7477 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7478","Abu Abdullah Al-Saffar told us, Abu Ismail Al-Sulami told us, and Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told me, regarding what I read to him about The origin of his book is that Al-Hasan bin Ali bin Ziyad informed us, saying: Abdul Aziz bin Abdullah Al-Uwaisi told us, Abu Musa Isa bin Abdullah Al-Khayyat, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, may God be pleased with him, that the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “The cup in the middle of the head is a sign of insanity, leprosy, drowsiness, and molars.” He used to call it “Savior.” “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration.” And they did not bring it out.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7478 - Jesus in the weak by Ibn Hibban and Ibn Adi"
"7479","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Sulaiman Al-Zahid told us, Ali bin Al-Hussein bin Al-Junaid Al-Razi, Ja’far bin Muhammad Al-Faryabi, and Zakaria bin Yahya Al-Saji, they said: Abu Al-Khattab Ziyad bin Yahya Al-Hasani told us, Ghazal bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadah, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them both, Nafi’ said: Ibn Umar said to me: I want a cupper who should not be a young boy or an old man, for the blood has turned white. By me, I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Cupping increases the mind and increases memory, so in the name of God on Thursday there is no They cupped on Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, and they cupped on Monday and Tuesday, and neither leprosy nor leprosy came down except during the night. “Wednesday” The narrators of this hadith are all trustworthy, except for Ghazal bin Muhammad, who is unknown, and I do not know him with justice or trustworthiness. The hadith was authenticated on the authority of Ibn Umar, may God be pleased with them, from his statement without a chain of transmission or a connection.
["
"7480","Abu Ali Al-Hafiz told us, Abdan Al-Ahwazi told us, Muhammad bin Omar bin Ali Al-Muqaddami told us, Abdullah bin Hisham told us Al-Dastawi, my father told me, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’, he said: Ibn Umar said to me: “O Nafi’, go and bring me a cupper and do not bring me an old man.” Not even a young boy.” And he said: “Under cupping on Saturday and cupping on Sunday, Monday and Tuesday, but do not cup on Wednesday.” This hadith was transmitted by Attaf bin Khaled Al-Makhzoumi, on the authority of Nafi’.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7480 - Abdullah bin Hisham Al-Dastawi is abandoned"
"7481","Abu Al-Nadr Al-Faqih and Abu Al-Hasan Al-Anazi narrated to us, saying: Othman bin Saeed Al-Darimi narrated to us, Abdullah bin Saleh Al-Masry narrated to us, Attaf bin Khaled, on the authority of Nafi’, that Abdullah bin Omar, may God be pleased with them both, said to him: O Nafi’, my blood has become excessive, so bring me a cup that is not An old man or a young boy, for I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Cupping on an empty stomach is better, and in it there is healing and blessing. It increases reason, increases memory, and increases the memory of the memorizer. So whoever uses cupping in the name of God, let him use cupping on Thursday and avoid Cupping on Friday, Saturday, and Sunday, and cupping on Monday and Tuesday, for that is the day that God has averted. Job is afflicted with affliction, and avoid cupping on Wednesday, for that is the day on which God afflicted Ayoub with affliction, and neither leprosy nor leprosy appear. Except on Wednesday or Wednesday night.”"
"7482","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub Al-Shaybani told us, Ibrahim bin Abdullah Al-Saadi told us, Muhammad bin Al-Qasim Al-Asadi told us, Al-Rabi’ told us Ibn Subaih, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Anas, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “When the heat becomes intense, seek help.” “By cupping, do not shed the blood of any of you lest it kill him.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7482 - True"
"7483","Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Hafid told us, Al-Hussein bin Al-Fadl told us, Abu Al-Nadr Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Al-Marja bin Raja Al-Yashkari, Abbad bin Mansour told me, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “What an excellent servant is the cupper, he lightens the back and sharpens the sight.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7483 - True"
"7484","Abu Zakaria Al-Anbari, Abu Bakr bin Ja’far Al-Muzaki, Abdullah bin Saad Al-Hafiz, and Ali bin Issa Al-Hairi told us, they said: Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Ibrahim Al-Abdi told us, Suleiman bin Abdul Rahman Al-Dimashqi told us, Al-Walid bin Muslim told us, Ibn Jurayj told us, On the authority of Amr bin Shuaib, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, he said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever seeks medicine and no medicine is known from him, is “Guarantor” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7484 - True"
"7485","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Abdul-Hakam told us, Ibn Wahb told me, Muawiyah told me Ibn Salih, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Jubayr ibn Nufayr, on the authority of Awf ibn Malik al-Ashja’i, who said: We used to recite ruqyah in pre-Islamic times, so we said: Oh Messenger of God, how do you think about that? He said: “Show me your ruqyah. There is no harm in ruqyah as long as it is not polytheism.” This hadith has an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7485 - True"
"7486","Ubayd Allah ibn Muhammad al-Balkhi told me, Abu Ismail Muhammad ibn Ismail told me, Muhammad ibn Wahb ibn Attiya al-Sulami told us, Muhammad ibn Harb, Muhammad ibn al-Walid al-Zubaidi told us, al-Zuhri told us, on the authority of Urwa ibn al-Zubayr, on the authority of Zainab bint Abi Salamah, on the authority of Umm Salamah, May God be pleased with her. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, saw a maid in her house who had a scald on her face, so he said: “Be careful for her, for she is affected by it.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7486 - It was included by Al-Bukhari"
"7487","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Abdul Rabbuh bin Saeed, Al-Minhal bin Amr told me, Saeed bin Jubayr told me, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. About them, he said: When the sick person returned, the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, would sit at his head and then say seven times: “I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Throne.” It is great that He heals you” and if there was a delay in it, then He will be relieved of that pain. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. No one followed Amr bin Al-Harith between Saeed and Ibn Abbas. Rather, it was narrated by Hajjaj bin Artaat, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, and Sa`id bin Jubayr was not mentioned among them.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7487 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7488","Al-Hasan bin Yaqoub Al-Adl told us, Yahya bin Abi Talib told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Hajjaj bin Artaat told us, about Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, on the authority of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: “Whoever returns He was sick, so he said, “I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Magnificent Throne, to heal you for a week, and if not his time has come.” It was narrated by Abu Khaled. Al-Dalani, and Maysarah bin Habib Al-Nahdi, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas"
"7489","So Abdul Rahman bin Al-Hasan Al-Qadi told us, Ibrahim bin Al-Hussein told us, Adam bin Abi Iyas told us, Shu’bah told us, and Abu told us Bakr Muhammad bin Ahmad bin Balawayh told us, Abdullah bin Ahmed bin Hanbal told us, my father told me, Muhammad bin Jaafar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, On the authority of Yazid bin Abi Khalid Al-Dalani, he said: I heard Al-Minhal bin Amr, speaking on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with him. On the authority of them, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, he said: “No Muslim servant visits a sick person who has not attended his death and says seven times, ‘I ask God Almighty. May the Lord of the Mighty Throne heal you, unless he is pardoned.”"
"7490","Abu Bakr bin Abi Darim Al-Hafiz narrated to us, in Kufa, Ahmad bin Musa narrated to us, Al-Ashja’i narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Maysara Al-Nahdi, On the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: “Who He came to see a sick person whose death had not come, and he said, “I ask God Almighty, Lord of the Mighty Throne, to heal you, except Aufy.”"
"7491","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Nadr told us, and Abu Zaid Saeed bin Al-Rabi’ told us, they said: We Shu’bah, on the authority of Qatada, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, who said: “The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, forbade ironing.” So we were defeated, but we did not succeed, nor did we succeed. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7491 - True"
"7492","Abu Amr Uthman bin Ahmad Al-Daqqaq told us, Al-Hasan bin Salam Al-Siwaq told us, Abu Asim told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah, said: A man from the Ansar was struck by a severe illness, and he was prescribed cauterization, so they came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So he turned away from them, then they came to him and he turned away from them, then he said on the third - or on the fourth -: “If you wish, be kind to him.” This is a hadith. It is authentic according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7492 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7493","Abu Zakaria al-Anbari told us, Ibrahim bin Abi Talib told us, Abd al-Quddus bin Muhammad al-Habhabi told me, Amr bin Asim told me, Hammam narrated to us, Qatada narrated to us, on the authority of Mutarrif bin Abdullah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn, that he said: “The angels did not greet me until he departed from me.” “The Effect of Fire” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7493 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7494","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Ahmad bin Abdul-Jabbar told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash told us, and Abu Abd told us God is the Protector, Muhammad bin Abdul Wahhab told us, Ali bin Ubaid told us, Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Jabir, may God be pleased with him. He said: “Ubayy bin Ka’b fell ill, may God be pleased with him, so the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent a doctor to him, who cut off a vein from him and then ironed it over it.” This An authentic hadith according to the conditions of a Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7494 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7495","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Yunus told me, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Abu Umamah bin Sahl bin Hanif, may God be pleased with him, said that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, returned Saad bin Zurarah with a thorn, so when he entered Accordingly, he said: “How miserable this dead person is. The Jews say, ‘If I had not paid for him, I would not own anything for him, nor would I own anything for myself, and they would not blame Abu Umamah.’” So Fukui ordered him to be killed, and he died. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, if Abu Umamah was among their companions and they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7495 - according to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7496","Abu Sahl bin Ziyad told us, Yahya bin Ja’far bin Al-Zabarqan told us, Abu Dawud told us, Shu’bah told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abd. Al-Rahman bin Zurarah said: I heard Omar, and I did not see any of us like him, saying that Saad bin Zurarah was struck by a pain, and the people called him Medina, the slaughter, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, cauterized him and he died. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “He died. It is bad for the Jews. They would say, ‘If only “It was paid for by its owner, and I do not own anything for him nor do I own anything.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7496 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7497","Ismail bin Muhammad bin Ismail al-Faqih told us about irrigation, Abu Hatim told us, Ahmad bin Ishaq al-Hadrami told us, Wahib told us, Abu Waqid Al-Laythi narrated to us, saying: I heard Abu Salamah bin Abdul-Rahman narrating on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: “Seek refuge in God Almighty from the evil eye, for the evil eye is real.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it in this manner. They only agreed on the hadith of Ibn Abbas: “The eye is true.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7497 - According to the conditions of Al-Bukhari and Muslim"
"7498","Ahmad bin Muhammad al-Muqri informed us, Othman bin Saeed al-Darimi told us, Ali bin al-Madini told us, Abd al-Rahman bin Mahdi told us, Sufyan, on the authority of Duraid, on the authority of Ismail ibn Thawban, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, may God be pleased with them both, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: “The eye is a truth that brings down the throat.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not include it with this addition.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7498 - True"
"7499","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Muhammad bin Ishaq Al-Saghani told us, Abu Al-Jawab told us, Ammar bin Ruzaq told us, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Issa, on the authority of Umayyah Ibn Hind, on the authority of Abdullah Ibn Amir Ibn Rabi’ah, on the authority of his father, may God be pleased with him, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: “If one of you sees of himself and his brother something that he likes, let him pray for blessing, for the evil eye is true.” This is an authentic hadith. The chain of transmission and they did not mention it by mentioning the blessing.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7499 - True"
"7500","Ali bin Issa Al-Hiri informed us, Muhammad bin Amr Al-Nadr Al-Jurashi told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Waki’ bin Al-Jarrah bin Malih, my father told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Issa, on the authority of Umayyah bin Hind bin Saad bin Sahil bin Hanif, on the authority of Abdullah bin Aamir bin Rabia, he said: Sahl bin Hunaif and Amer bin Rabia went out with him, wanting to wash themselves. They ended up at Ghadir, and Sahl came out wanting alcohol - he said. Waki’: meaning a cover - until when he saw that he had taken off a cloak of wool over him, put it on and then entered the water, he said: I looked at him and hit him. With my own eyes, I heard him frolicking in the water, so I went to him and called him three times, but he did not answer me. So I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and told him, and he started walking. He waded through the water until it was as if I could see the whites of his legs, and he stroked his chest and then said: “O God, remove from him its heat and cold and pour it on.” Then he stood up and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you sees for himself, his property, or his brother what he likes, let him bless him, for the evil eye is valid.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7500 - True"
"7501","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Haywa told me, on the authority of Khaled bin Ubaid. Al-Maafiri, on the authority of Musharrah bin Ha’an, that he heard Uqba bin Amir, may God be pleased with him, say: I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, say: “Whoever wears an amulet, God will not complete it for him, and whoever wears an amulet, God will not complete it.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, and they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7501 - True"
"7502","Ahmad bin Sulaiman Al-Faqih told us, Al-Hasan bin Makram told us, Othman bin Omar told us, Abu Amir Saleh bin Rustom told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, On the authority of Imran bin Husayn, may God be pleased with him, he said: I entered upon the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and there was a yellow ring on my upper arm, and he said: “What is this?” So I said: From the weak one. He said: “Throw it away.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7502 - True"
"7503","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi told us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Ubayd Allah bin Musa told us, Ibn Abi Laila told us, about His brother, Issa, said: I entered upon Abu Ma`abad al-Juhani, who is Abdullah ibn Hakim, and he had coals of coals, and I said: Don’t you hang anything? He said: Death is closer than that. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “Whoever becomes attached to something and is entrusted to it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7503 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7504","Bakr bin Muhammad al-Sayrifi told us, with Marwa, Abd al-Samad bin al-Fadl told us, Makki bin Ibrahim told us, al-Sari bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Duha, on the authority of Umm Najiya, who said: I entered upon Zainab, the wife of Abdullah, seeking refuge in her from an ember that appeared on her face while she was hanging on a rope. As I was sitting, Abdullah came in, and when he looked at the guard, he came to a stranger in the house and put his cloak on him, then he wrapped his arms around him. So he came to her, took the guard and pulled her until her face almost fell on the ground, but it broke off. Then he left the house and said: It has become Abdullah is free from polytheism, then he went out and threw it behind the wall and then said: O Zainab, do you want me to comment that I heard the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him? He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: “He forbade ruqyahs, amulets, and guardianship.” Umm Najiya said: O Abu Abdul Rahman, as for ruqyahs and amulets, we know So what is guardianship? He said: Guardianship is what excites women.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7504 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7505","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Abdullah Al-Zahid Al-Asbahani told us, Ahmad bin Mihran told us, Ubaid Allah bin Musa told us, Israel told us, On the authority of Maysarah bin Habib, on the authority of Al-Minhal bin Amr, on the authority of Qais bin Al-Sakan Al-Asadi, who said: Abdullah bin Masoud, may God be pleased with him, entered On a woman, and he saw on her a reddish mark, so he cut her violently, then said: Indeed, the family of Abdullah are wealthy from polytheism, and he said: It was among the We have learned from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, “Indeed, spells, amulets, and friendship are from polytheism.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7505 - True"
"7506","Abu Al-Abbas Al-Sayyari told us, Abu Al-Mujih told us, Abdullah told us, Talha bin Abi Saeed told me, on the authority of Bukayr bin Abdul Allah bin Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, said: “The amulet is not what is attached to it after affliction, but rather “The amulet is something that was attached to it before the calamity.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, but they did not narrate it.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7506 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7507","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me, on the authority of Bukayr Ibn Abdullah Ibn Al-Ashjaj, on the authority of Al-Qasim Ibn Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, may God be pleased with her, who said: “The amulet is not what has been attached to it yet.” “The amulet is that which was attached to it before the calamity.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two sheikhs, and they did not narrate it. “Perhaps someone is delusional and imagines that it is one of the The rulings on Aisha, may God be pleased with her, and that is not the case, as the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, mentioned amulets in many reports, so if Aisha, may God be pleased with her, explained the amulet, for it is a hadith with a chain of narration.
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7507 - True"
"7508","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Wahb told us, Amr bin Al-Harith told me that Bukayr, He told him that his mother told him that she had sent to Aisha, may God be pleased with her, Makhramah for his brother, and she was being treated for an ulcer that was With the boys. When Aisha treated him and finished with him, she saw two new anklets on his feet. Aisha said: “Did you think that these The two anklets protect him from something that God has decreed for him. If I had seen them, they would not have been cured by me and they would not have touched me in my lifetime, for two anklets of purer silver. Of these two: “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7508 - Al-Dhahabi deleted it from the summary"
"7509","Sheikh Abu Bakr bin Ishaq told us, Ismail bin Qutaibah told us, Yahya bin Yahya told us, Abu Muawiyah told us, Al-Amash, on the authority of Shaqiq, said: A man complained about his stomach being yellow, and he was described as drunk. He mentioned that to Abdullah, and he said: “Indeed, God Almighty did not He will make your cure for what has been forbidden to you.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7509 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7510","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Yaqoub told us, Bahr bin Nasr told us, Abdullah bin Al-Harith told us, Amr bin Wahb told me that Abdul Rabbuh bin Saeed told him that he heard Nafi’, saying: “Whenever Ibn Umar invited a doctor to treat some of his companions, he stipulated that he not It can be treated with something that God Almighty has forbidden.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7510 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7511","Abd al-Rahman bin Hamdan al-Jallab told us about Hamdan, Ibrahim bin Nasr told us, Harami bin Hisn told us, Abd al-Aziz bin Muslim, Muhammad bin Amr bin Abi Salamah narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, may God be pleased with him, who said: The wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, came and mentioned That there is a sect of Satan in it, and the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If you wish, I may call upon God Almighty and He will heal you, and if you wish, there is no reckoning or Torment.” She said: O Messenger of God, then leave me alone. “This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of Muslim, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7511 - According to Muslim’s condition"
"7512","Taher bin Muhammad bin Al-Hussein Al-Bayhaqi told me, Khali Al-Fadl bin Muhammad bin Al-Musayyab told us, Saeed bin Abi Maryam told us, Al-Layth bin Saad, Ziyad bin Muhammad Al-Ansari told me, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ka’b Al-Qurazi, on the authority of Fadalah bin Ubaid, that he said: Two men from the people of Iraqis seeking recovery for a father whose urine had been withheld, so the people showed him some leftovers. The two men came with some leftovers, and he mentioned who was bringing them. Fadalah said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, saying: “Whoever complains about something among you, or a brother of his complains, let him say: Our Lord, who is in Heaven, hallowed be your name. Your command in heaven and earth, just as your mercy was in heaven and earth. Forgive us our debts and our sins, O Lord of the good. Send down healing. By Your healing and mercy on this pain, he will be cured. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7512 - True"
"7513","Abu Ishaq Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Yahya told us, the Imam of the Muslims Abu Bakr Muhammad bin Ishaq bin Khuzaymah told us, may God be pleased with him. On his authority, Muhammad ibn Musa al-Hurashi narrated to us, Sahl ibn Aslam al-Adawi narrated to us, Yazid ibn Abi Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of the two men, on the authority of Uqba ibn Amer Al-Juhani said that he came with ten people to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and pledged allegiance to nine of them, but withheld the pledge of allegiance to one of them. They said: What? Why don't you pledge allegiance to this man? He said: “Indeed, there is an amulet on his arm.” The man cut the amulet, so the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, pledged allegiance to him. Then he said: “Whoever is attached has committed polytheism.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7513 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
"7514","Abu Al-Abbas Muhammad bin Ahmad Al-Mahboubi informed us, Saeed bin Masoud told us, Yazid bin Harun told us, Al-Jariri informed us, on the authority of Abu Al-Alaa, on the authority of Othman bin Abi Al-Aas, may God be pleased with him, who said: I said: O Messenger of God, Satan has come between me and my prayer and reading, so he said: “Indeed That is a devil called a demon, so if you sense him, seek refuge in God from him and spit to your left. He said: So I did, and God went away from me. “This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7514 - True"
"7515","Ali ibn Hamshadh al-Adl told us, Musa ibn Harun told us, Abd al-Warith ibn Abd al-Samad told us, my father told me, Abu Matar Muhammad ibn Salem, Thabit Al-Bunani narrated to us, he said: “If you complain, put your hand where you complain, then say: In the name of God, I seek refuge in God’s glory and power from evil.” What pain do I find in this? Then raise your hand, then count this as a string. Anas bin Malik said: He told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace Tell him about that.” This is a hadith with an authentic chain of narration, but they did not narrate it.”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7515 - True"
"7516","Abu Abdullah Muhammad bin Yaqoub bin Yusuf Al-Hafiz told us, my father told us, Qutaibah bin Saeed told us, Abdul Wahhab bin Abdul Majeed said: I heard Yahya bin Saeed saying: Muhammad bin Abdul Rahman bin Haritha told me, on the authority of Amra, that Aisha, May God be pleased with her. She was afflicted with an illness, and some of her nephews mentioned that she complained to a man about his oils, and that he said to them: They... They will mention a bewitched woman whose maid bewitched her and a boy in her lap. In the maid’s lap now is a boy who urinated in her lap and said: Eat me. With it. She was brought and Aisha said: “Did you bewitch me?” She said: Yes, she said: “Why?” She said: I wanted to be emancipated, and Aisha, may God be pleased with her, had emancipated her some time ago, so she said: “It is for God’s sake that you not be emancipated.” “Never see the worst of the houses being owned and sold to them, then they bought a slave for its price and freed her.” This is an authentic hadith according to the conditions of the two Sheikhs, and it was not It is published by “the last book of medicine”
[Commentary - from Al-Dhahabi’s summary] 7516 - Al-Dhahabi remained silent about it in his summary"
